id: 37
hanzi: 根
pinyin: gēn
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Measure Word

meanings_summary:
  en: measure word for slender, fibrous, or cylindrical objects; root; origin; foundation
  es: clasificador para objetos delgados y alargados; raíz; origen; cimiento

senses[2]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Measure Word | Standard | used to count long, slender, fibrous, or rod-like objects such as ropes, arrows, needles, pillars, or hairs | clasificador para contar cosas alargadas, finas o cilíndricas como cuerdas, flechas, agujas o cabellos | 一根绳子 (a rope)
  2 | Noun | Standard | the underground part of a plant absorbing nutrients; the foundation, source, or origin of a matter | parte subterránea de las plantas; base, raíz u origen de un asunto | 树根 (tree root)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 李广将军再度发箭，结果几根坚韧的箭杆接连折断，箭头纷纷碎裂跌落在冰冷的乱石堆中。 | Lǐ Guǎng jiāngjūn zàidù fājiàn, jiéguǒ jǐ gēn jiānrèn de jiàngǎn jiēlián zhéduàn, jiàntóu fēnfēn suìliè diēluò zài bīnglěng de luànshíduī zhōng. | General Li Guang shot again, but several tough arrow shafts snapped in succession, arrowheads shattering into the cold scree. | El general Li Guang disparó de nuevo, pero varias varas resistentes de saeta se quebraron seguidas, cayendo las puntas rotas entre el pedregal.
  #2 | 传统文化是中华民族生生不息的精神根基，唯有深深扎根于人民生活的沃土，文艺创作才能焕发出恒久生命力。 | Chuántǒng wénhuà shì Zhōnghuá mínzú shēngshēng-bùxī de jīngshén gēnjī, wéiyǒu shēnshēn zhāgēn yú rénmín shēnghuó de wòtǔ, wényì chuàngzuò cáinéng huànfā chū héngjiǔ shēngmìnglì. | Traditional culture is the enduring spiritual root of the Chinese nation; only by rooting in the people's fertile soil can artistic creation flourish. | La cultura tradicional es el arraigo espiritual de la nación china; solo hundiéndose en la tierra fecunda del pueblo logrará el arte una vitalidad imperecedera.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  一根绳子 | a rope (classifier: 根)
  一根筷子 | a chopstick
  一根针 | a needle
  深扎树根 | deeply rooted tree roots
  根本原因 | root cause; fundamental reason
  寻根问底 | probe to the root and origin

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  根深蒂固 | gēn shēn dì gù | deep-rooted and firmly established; ingrained
  寻根究底 | xún gēn jiū dǐ | probe to the very bottom and origin of an issue
  落叶归根 | luò yè guī gēn | fallen leaves return to the roots; revert to one's origins
  盘根错节 | pán gēn cuò jié | twisted roots and gnarled branches; intricate and complicated

character_decomposition[1]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  根 | gēn | root; foundation; origin; measure word | raíz; origen; cimiento; clasificador | 木 | tree / wood | 木 (tree, botanical root) | 艮 (gèn, stop / turning eye) | 10 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound: tree radical 木 denoting botanical roots anchoring in earth, paired with 艮 (firmly standing still). | The sturdy trunk of a tree (木) anchors itself firmly into the soil (艮) through branching underground roots (根). | El tronco del árbol (木) se aferra con firmeza a la tierra (艮) a través de sus profundas raíces (根). | 55 | DAHV | 

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: The underground anchors of a tree (木) holding firm in the soil (艮) establish roots (根) and count long slender shafts (根).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Los anclajes de un árbol (木) que se aferran firmes al suelo (艮) forjan las raíces (根) y cuentan varas y ramas (根).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In ancient agrarian thought, 根 represents the subterranean anchor of life and the metaphysical wellspring of human existence (归根结底, 根基). From plant roots, it extended to categorize slender botanical fibers and flexible linear implements.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: High level 1st tone 'gēn' (55). Pronounced with an even, sustained, clear high vocal acoustic.

