semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 根 is a versatile measure word for flexible or natural slender cylindrical items (ropes, needles, shafts), and a noun for roots.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 根 vs. 支 | zhī | 根 is preferred for flexible or natural fibrous slender items (一根绳子, 一根头发, 一根香蕉), whereas 支 is preferred for rigid manufactured tools (一支笔, 一支箭, 一支枪).
    2 | 根 vs. 条 | tiáo | 根 emphasizes thinness and straight cylindrical shape (一根针), while 条 emphasizes long, undulating flexibility (一条蛇, 一条河, 一条裤子).
    3 | 根 vs. 蒂 | dì | 根 is the underground nourishing anchor, while 蒂 is the stem or pedicel attaching fruits or flowers to branches.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 参天大树之所以能历经千百年的狂风暴雨而屹立不倒，全赖其深深扎入沃土之中的粗壮盘根。每一根幼细的须根都在暗夜中奋力汲取大地的滋养。唯有把根扎得足够深，生命方能枝繁叶茂、昂然挺立于天地之间。 | Cāntiān dàshù zhīsuǒyǐ néng lìjīng qiānbǎi nián de kuángfēng-bàoyǔ ér yìlì-bùdǎo, quán lài qí shēnshēn zhārù wòtǔ zhīzhōng de cūzhuàng pángēn. Měi yì gēn yòuxì de xūgēn dōu zài ànyè zhōng fènlì jíqǔ dàdì de zīyǎng. Wéiyǒu bǎ gēn zhā de zúgòu shēn, shēngmìng fāng néng zhīfán-yèmào, ángrán tǐnglì yú tiāndì zhījiān. | Why giant trees withstand centuries of storms without falling relies entirely on massive roots plunged deep into soil. Every tiny rootlet draws nourishment in dark earth. Only by rooting deep does life flourish toward the skies. | Si los árboles colosales resisten siglos de vendavales sin caer es gracias a sus recias raíces hundidas en la tierra. Cada fina hebra absorbe savia en la oscuridad; solo enraizando hondo puede la vida erguirse lozana entre el cielo y el suelo.
  #2 | 在传承弘扬中华优秀传统文化的宏伟工程中，我们要善于从历史文化脉络中寻找中华民族现代文明的精神之根。唯有守护好文化根脉，才能在汹涌澎湃的全球化浪潮中保持坚定的文化自信，谱写当代华章。 | Zài chuánchéng hóngyáng Zhōnghuá yōuxiù chuántǒng wénhuà de hóngwěi gōngchéng zhōng, wǒmen yào shànyú cóng lìshǐ wénhuà màiluò zhōng xúnzhǎo Zhōnghuá mínzú xiàndài wénmíng de jīngshén zhī gēn. Wéiyǒu shǒuhù hǎo wénhuà gēnmài, cáinéng zài xiōngyǒng-péngpài de quánqiúhuà làngcháo zhōng bǎochí jiāndìng de wénhuà zìxìn, pǔxiě dāngdài huázhāng. | In carrying forward traditional culture, we must discover the spiritual roots of modern civilization in historical veins. Guarding cultural rootlines preserves unwavering self-confidence amid globalizing tides, composing modern anthems. | Al preservar el legado cultural tradicional, debemos rastrear las raíces espirituales de la civilización moderna en los anales patrios. Custodiar el arraigo cultural preserva la identidad ante las mareas globales, alumbrando un porvenir fecundo.
